 "description_summary": "A beautifully restored 1911 Craftsman just one block from Manito Park. Three bedrooms, two bathrooms, a fenced backyard for dogs, and a fully stocked kitchen in Spokane’s most walkable neighborhood. Work from the dedicated desk with a 32\" monitor, unwind on the Article sofas by the fireplace, or walk to South Hill coffee shops and restaurants. Historic charm with every modern comfort you need.The spaceThis 1911 Craftsman bungalow has been thoughtfully restored to preserve its original character while adding everything a modern guest needs. Hardwood floors, period details, and a warm fireplace set the tone, while high-speed Wi-Fi, smart TVs, and a dedicated workspace keep you connected.  WHERE YOU’LL SLEEP  Primary Bedroom: Queen bed with plush linens Second Bedroom: King bed — the most popular room with guests Third Bedroom: Two full beds, great for kids or groups Upstairs Living Room: Full sleeper sofa for extra guests  LIVING & DINING  The main living room features a 75” Smart TV with a Sonos Beam soundbar (AirPlay-enabled), comfortable Article sofas, and a gas fireplace. Upstairs you’ll find a second living area with a 65” Smart TV — perfect when your group wants to split up. The farmhouse dining table seats six comfortably.  KITCHEN  Fully stocked with pots, pans, bakeware, wine glasses, and a FlexBrew coffee maker that works with both K-Cups and ground coffee. White cabinetry, warm butcher block countertops, and a stainless steel sink make cooking feel easy.  WORK FROM HERE  The primary bedroom includes a dedicated desk with a 32” monitor — a real workspace, not an afterthought. Pair it with the high-speed Wi-Fi and you’ve got a setup that’s better than most hotel business centers.  OUTDOOR SPACE  A large, fully fenced backyard is perfect for dogs and kids. The private driveway fits multiple cars, and there’s ample street parking for extra vehicles.  GETTING AROUND  Manito Park: 1 block (2-minute walk) South Hill coffee shops and restaurants: 5-minute walk Downtown Spokane: 10-minute drive Gonzaga University: 15-minute drive Spokane International Airport: 20-minute drive Providence Sacred Heart Medical Center: 12-minute drive Northern Quest Casino: 25-minute driveGuest accessYou’ll have full access to the main floor, upstairs, and the front and back yards. A private driveway is available for parking. The unfinished basement is the only area that’s off-limits.Other things to noteTraveling with little ones? A travel crib / pack ‘n play is available - just let us know and we’ll have it set up before you arrive. Please leave it unfolded after use so our cleaners can wash the sheets.  The backyard is fully fenced and pet-friendly. We welcome well-behaved dogs!  A few house rules to keep things great for everyone: – No smoking indoors. You’re welcome to smoke on the front or back porch; please dispose of butts in the provided receptacle. – No parties or events. – Quiet hours after 10 PM out of respect for the neighbors",
 "description_full": [
  {
   "section": null,
   "text": "A beautifully restored 1911 Craftsman just one block from Manito Park. Three bedrooms, two bathrooms, a fenced backyard for dogs, and a fully stocked kitchen in Spokane’s most walkable neighborhood. Work from the dedicated desk with a 32\" monitor, unwind on the Article sofas by the fireplace, or walk to South Hill coffee shops and restaurants. Historic charm with every modern comfort you need."
  },
  {
   "section": "The space",
   "text": "This 1911 Craftsman bungalow has been thoughtfully restored to preserve its original character while adding everything a modern guest needs. Hardwood floors, period details, and a warm fireplace set the tone, while high-speed Wi-Fi, smart TVs, and a dedicated workspace keep you connected.  WHERE YOU’LL SLEEP  Primary Bedroom: Queen bed with plush linens Second Bedroom: King bed — the most popular room with guests Third Bedroom: Two full beds, great for kids or groups Upstairs Living Room: Full sleeper sofa for extra guests  LIVING & DINING  The main living room features a 75” Smart TV with a Sonos Beam soundbar (AirPlay-enabled), comfortable Article sofas, and a gas fireplace. Upstairs you’ll find a second living area with a 65” Smart TV — perfect when your group wants to split up. The farmhouse dining table seats six comfortably.  KITCHEN  Fully stocked with pots, pans, bakeware, wine glasses, and a FlexBrew coffee maker that works with both K-Cups and ground coffee. White cabinetry, warm butcher block countertops, and a stainless steel sink make cooking feel easy.  WORK FROM HERE  The primary bedroom includes a dedicated desk with a 32” monitor — a real workspace, not an afterthought. Pair it with the high-speed Wi-Fi and you’ve got a setup that’s better than most hotel business centers.  OUTDOOR SPACE  A large, fully fenced backyard is perfect for dogs and kids. The private driveway fits multiple cars, and there’s ample street parking for extra vehicles.  GETTING AROUND  Manito Park: 1 block (2-minute walk) South Hill coffee shops and restaurants: 5-minute walk Downtown Spokane: 10-minute drive Gonzaga University: 15-minute drive Spokane International Airport: 20-minute drive Providence Sacred Heart Medical Center: 12-minute drive Northern Quest Casino: 25-minute drive"
  },
  {
   "section": "Guest access",
   "text": "You’ll have full access to the main floor, upstairs, and the front and back yards. A private driveway is available for parking. The unfinished basement is the only area that’s off-limits."
  },
  {
   "section": "Other things to note",
   "text": "Traveling with little ones? A travel crib / pack ‘n play is available - just let us know and we’ll have it set up before you arrive. Please leave it unfolded after use so our cleaners can wash the sheets.  The backyard is fully fenced and pet-friendly. We welcome well-behaved dogs!  A few house rules to keep things great for everyone: – No smoking indoors. You’re welcome to smoke on the front or back porch; please dispose of butts in the provided receptacle. – No parties or events. – Quiet hours after 10 PM out of respect for the neighbors"
  }
 ],
